TABLE	function pointer	Kani
Parse	function pointer	Kani
Read	function pointer	Kani
read_slot	raw pointer from C caller	Miri (evidence only)
byte_at	raw pointer from C caller	Miri (evidence only)
bytes_at	raw pointer from C caller	Miri (evidence only)
environ_array	raw pointer from C caller	Miri (evidence only)
# Termination of the `environ` walk: the C program ends the array with a null pointer.
env_var	C-program contract	none (assumption)
# `CStr` literals, which Verus does not take: Verus sees each only as a
# value of its type (the whole contract). The const asserts pin the
# spelling of each name in every build.
THP_NAMES	core library	Kani	discharged (const assert: `THP_NAMES` in src/config.rs)
PERCPU_ARENA_NAMES	core library	Kani	discharged (const assert: `PERCPU_ARENA_NAMES` in src/config.rs)
# Built from `TABLE`, which holds function pointers; claimed only as a value of its type.
KEYS	function pointer	Kani	discharged (Kani: config::kani_config::keys_are_the_table_names)
# Checked by the Kani harnesses the status names (verus/README.md, "Kani").
Config::set_listed	function pointer	Kani	discharged (Kani: config::kani_config::set_listed_contract)
Config::get	function pointer	Kani	trusted (partly checked, Kani: config::kani_config::get_contract; not checked: the real `Thp::name` and `PercpuArena::name`, which the harness stubs (they index the `CStr` tables `THP_NAMES` and `PERCPU_ARENA_NAMES`; Kani 0.68 has no C string literals))
# Inline assembly checked with Isla (verus/ISLA.md): run.sh checks
# each against the contract verus/isla/seams.md quotes.
malloc_conf_addr	inline asm	Islaris/Isla	discharged (Isla: verus/isla/seams.md)
je_malloc_conf_addr	inline asm	Islaris/Isla	discharged (Isla: verus/isla/seams.md)
